    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Electricity and Magnetism",
    "chapter": "AC Circuits",
    "topic": "AC Impedance",
    "subtopic": "Calculation of Impedance",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"notes-image-container my-4 text-center flex flex-col items-center\"><center><img src=\"https://onedrive.live.com/embed?resid=9C913AE725AFDEB1%21532&authkey=%21AJPy5jCikLXe0Qs&width=340\" width=\"340\"/></center></div><p>While calculating Impedance (equivalent of resistance in AC circuits)</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Resistance is plotted on x-axis as it is, going towards right direction.</li>\r\n\t<li>Inductance is calculated using the following formula and plotted vertically upwards. <span class=\"math display\">\\[X_{L} = 2 \\pi f L = \\omega L\\]</span></li>\r\n\t<li>Capacitance is calculated using the following formula and plotted vertically downwards. <span class=\"math display\">\\[X_{C} = \\dfrac{1}{2 \\pi f C} = \\dfrac{1}{\\omega C}\\]</span>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>So, the combined effect of inductance and capacitance Reactance is plotted on y-axis by taking the difference of <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\displaystyle X_{L}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\displaystyle X_{C}\\)</span>. <span class=\"math display\">\\[X = X_L - X_C\\]</span> Impedance is calculated using Pythagoras theorem <span class=\"math display\">\\[Z = \\sqrt{R^{2} + (X_{L} - X_{C})^{2}}\\]</span></p>",
    "important": "\\[V = V_{max}\\ \\sin \\omega t\\]\r\n\r\n\\[X_{L} = 2 \\pi f L = \\omega L\\]\r\n\r\n\\[X_{C} = \\dfrac{1}{2 \\pi f C} = \\dfrac{1}{\\omega C}\\]\r\n\\[X = X_L - X_C\\]\r\n\r\n\\[Z = \\sqrt{R^{2} + (X_{L} - X_{C})^{2}}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hieR0xwD8YpW95Quz7hqfwlRoVPMMEd4/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1aHVzaKDq6O_iGTjN-ptWhbf9Tm-VnTdt/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1I1nGDYsJ3noRY30d0h_Mxg2k4wfPKYN0/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
