    "subtopic": "Power Factor and Power Angle",
    "content_html": "<p>Power angle <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> is the angle between Z and R. Power factor = cos<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\phi\\)</span>.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>For purely resistive circuit, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> = 0 and power factor = 1.</li>\r\n\t<li>For purely inductive circuit, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> = 90$^\\circ$ and power factor = 0.</li>\r\n\t<li>For purely capacitive circuit, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\phi\\)</span> = -90$^\\circ$ and power factor = 0.</li>\r\n</ul>",
