    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-6\">\r\n<p><strong>Electric current</strong> is defined as the rate at which charge flows through a surface (such as cross section of a wire).</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$di(t) = \\dfrac{dq(t)}{dt}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 358</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>Or in stedy state format, <span class=\"math display\">\\[I = \\dfrac{Q}{t}\\]</span> I = electric current rate at which charge flows in a certain pathway<br />\r\nQ = amount of charge flowing past a certain point<br />\r\nt = time<br />\r\nSI unit for electric current:<br />\r\n1 Ampere = 1 Coulomb/1 second</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3f/ElectricCurrent.gif\" alt=\"ElectricCurrent\" width=\"500\"><br/>\r\n<center><small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ElectricCurrent.gif\">And1mu</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "\\[I = \\dfrac{Q}{t}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1npZPw9cScIsUboH78NKr3g3pVPHfg9GD/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VDwt5RsoCYrZpXxNgCWQdTpmDgvG2XUP/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a></div>",
