    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Fluid Mechanics",
    "chapter": "Impulse-Momentum Principle",
    "topic": "Deflectors and Blades",
    "subtopic": "Impulse Turbine",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   Power of the turbine is given by:\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dot{W} = Q \\rho (v_1 - v) (1 - \\cos \\alpha) v$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 189</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dot{W}_{max} = Q \\rho (\\dfrac{v_1^2}{4}) (1 - \\cos \\alpha)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 189</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nWhen $\\alpha$ = 180$^\\circ$\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dot{W}_{max} = Q \\rho (\\dfrac{v_1^2}{2}) = Q \\gamma (\\dfrac{v_1^2}{2g})$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 189</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c3/Nozzle_flow_case_3.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nozzle_flow_case_3.svg\">Olivier Cleynen</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
