    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Material Properties and Processing",
    "chapter": "Corrosion",
    "topic": "Corrosion Mechanism",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<p>Oxidation takes place at the surface of the metal forming metal ions <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\large M^{n+}\\]</span> <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\large M^{0}\\rightarrow M^{n+}+n e^{-}\\]</span> Oxygen is converted to oxide ion due to the transfer of electrons from metal. <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\large \\frac{n}{2}O_{2} +2n e^{-}\\rightarrow nO^{2-}\\]</span> The overall reaction is of oxide ion reacts with the metal ions to form metal oxide film. <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\large 2M + \\frac{n}{2}O_{2}\\rightarrow 2M^{n+}+ nO^{2-}\\]</span></p>",
    "important": "",
