    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Material Properties and Processing",
    "chapter": "Manufacturing Processes",
    "topic": "Powder Metallurgy",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-6\">\r\n<p>It is the type of manufacturing from powdered metals by placing these powders in molds and applying pressure. These compressed parts are then heated to bind the particles together and improve their strength and other properties. This process is called sintering. It involves:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Production of metal powders.</li>\r\n\t<li>Mixing or blending of the metal powders in required proportions.</li>\r\n\t<li>Pressing and compacting the powders into desired shapes and sizes.</li>\r\n\t<li>Sintering the compacted parts in a controlled furnace atmosphere.</li>\r\n\t<li>Subjecting the sintered parts to secondary processing, if required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n     <center><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/98/Rhodium_powder_pressed_melted.jpg\" alt=\"Rhodium powder pressed melted\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhodium_powder_pressed_melted.jpg\">Alchemist-hp (talk) www.pse-mendelejew.dederivative work: Purpy Pupple</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/de/deed.en\">CC BY-SA 3.0 DE</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
