    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Material Properties and Processing",
    "chapter": "Materials Selection",
    "topic": "Material Selection Factors",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Material Properties The expected level of performance from the material</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Material must be priced appropriately</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Availability</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Processing (Casting, Machining, Welding)</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>The effect the part and the processing has on the environment.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Design of an engineering component involves three interrelated problems:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Selecting a material: The choice of a material is frequently the result of several compromises. For example, the technical appraisal of an alloy will generally be a compromise between corrosion resistance and several other properties such as strength and weldability. And the final selection may come down to a compromise between technical and economic factors.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>specifying a shape, and</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>choosing a manufacturing process.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>When we talk about choosing materials for a component, we take into account many different factors. These factors can be broken down into the following areas:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Material Properties: The expected level of performance from the material.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Material Cost and Availability : Material must be priced appropriately and material must be available preferably from multiple sources.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Processing Must consider how to make the part, for example:</p>\r\n\r\n\t<ol>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>Casting</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>Machining</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>Welding</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t</ol>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Environment:</p>\r\n\r\n\t<ul>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>The effect that the service environment has on the part</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>The effect the part has on the environment</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t\t<li>\r\n\t\t<p>The effect that processing has on the environment</p>\r\n\t\t</li>\r\n\t</ul>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"sustainability\">Sustainability:</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Engineers should design and manufacture products, industrial plants, transportation, and infrastructure in such a way that natural resources and environment quality will not cross harmful level for future generations. Sustainability has three domains:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>economics</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>environment</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>social sustainability</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Green engineering</strong> is a subset of sustainable engineering. Green engineering involves four basic approaches to improve processes and products to make them more efficient from an environmental standpoint.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Waste reduction</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Materials management</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Pollution prevention</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Product enhancement</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>",
    "important": "",
