    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-6\">\r\n<p>The liquid-vapour equilibrium curve has a top limit which is known as the <strong>critical point</strong>. The temperature and pressure corresponding to this are known as the <strong>critical temperature</strong> and <strong>critical pressure</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n    <center><img src=\"https://onedrive.live.com/embed?resid=9C913AE725AFDEB1%21623&authkey=%21AAuLJU-ab_Emwmc&width=500\" width=\"500\"/></center>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
