    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Material Properties and Processing",
    "chapter": "Phase Diagrams/Heat Treating",
    "topic": "Phase Diagrams",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Gibbs Phase Rule:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p>In a system under a set of conditions, number of phases (P) exist can be related to the number of components (C) and degrees of freedom (F) by Gibbs phase rule.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$P + F = C+ 2$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 155</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nwhere, <br/>\r\nP = Number of phases making up a system<br/>\r\nF = Degrees of freedom<br/>\r\nC = Number of components in a system<br/>\r\n\r\n<p>Degrees of freedom refers to the number of independent variables (e.g.: pressure, temperature) that can be varied individually to effect changes in a system.</p>",
