    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Material Properties and Processing",
    "chapter": "Phase Diagrams/Heat Treating",
    "topic": "Triple Point",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>Where all three curves, solid, liquid and gas, meet, there is a unique combination of temperature and pressure where all three phases are in equilibrium together. This point is called a <strong>triple point</strong>.</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/30/Phase-diag.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phase-diag.svg\">Maksim</a>, <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
