    "chapter": "Linear Algebra",
    "topic": "Types of Matrices",
    "subtopic": "Identity Matrix",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Identity Matrix:</b></span></h5>\n<p>An <strong>Identity Matrix</strong> (or unit matrix) of size $n \\times n$ is a square matrix with ones on the main diagonal and zeros elsewhere.</p>\n<div class=\"marginfigure text-center my-3\">\n<p>\\[I_3 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0\\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}\\]</p>\n</div>\n<h5><span><b>Key Properties of Identity Matrix:</b></span></h5>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Multiplicative Identity:</strong> For any matrix $A$ of compatible dimension:\n    \\[A \\cdot I = I \\cdot A = A\\]\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Determinant:</strong> The determinant of an identity matrix is always $1$:\n    \\[\\det(I) = |I| = 1\\]\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Invertibility:</strong> The identity matrix is its own inverse:\n    \\[I^{-1} = I\\]\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Idempotent:</strong> Multiplying the identity matrix by itself yields the identity matrix:\n    \\[I^k = I \\quad \\text{for any integer } k \\geq 1\\]\n  </li>\n  <li><strong>Trace:</strong> The trace of an $n \\times n$ identity matrix equals its dimension $n$:\n    \\[\\text{tr}(I_n) = n\\]\n  </li>\n</ul>",
    "important": "Properties of Identity Matrix:\r\n\\[A \\cdot I = I \\cdot A = A\\]\r\n\\[|I| = 1,\\quad I^{-1} = I,\\quad I^k = I\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><!-- <div class=\"w-full mt-2\"><div style=\"padding:56.25% 0 0 0;position:relative;\"><iframe src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/833004456?h=edd07e38b9&amp;badge=0&amp;autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\" title=\"Types of Matrices\"></iframe></div><script src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js\"></script></div> --></div>",
