    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Measurements, Instrumentation and Controls",
    "chapter": "Data Acquisition",
    "topic": "Analog-to-Digital Converters",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-8\">\r\n   ADC (Analog to Digital Converter) is an electronic device that converts a continuous analog input signal to discrete digital numbers.\r\n\r\nImportance:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>All microcontrollers store information using digital logic.</li>\r\n<li>Compress information to digital form for efficient storage.</li>\r\n<li>Medium for storing digital data is more robust.</li>\r\n<li>Digital data transfer is more efficient.</li>\r\n<li>Digital data is easy to reproduce.</li>\r\n<li>Provide a link between real-world signals and data storage.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nTwo stages of ADC:\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Sampling</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Reduction of a continuous signal to a discrete signal</li>\r\n<li>Achieved through sampling and holding circuit</li>\r\n<li>Must hold sampled value constant for digital conversion.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li>Quantizing and Encoding</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approximates a continuous range of values and replaces it with a binary number</li>\r\n<li>Error is introduced between in put voltage and outpur binary representation.</li>\r\n<li>Error depends upon the resolution of the ADC.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\nTypes of ADC:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Flash ADC</li>\r\n<li>Successive approximation ADC</li>\r\n<li>Dual Slope ADC</li>\r\n<li>Delta-Sigma ADC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Delta-Sigma_Modulation_ADC_and_DAC.svg\" style=\"width:500px;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Delta-Sigma_Modulation_ADC_and_DAC.svg\">Em3rgent0rdr</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "",
    "images": [],
    "local_images": []
