    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Measurements, Instrumentation and Controls",
    "chapter": "Data Acquisition",
    "topic": "Filtering",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "In order to eliminate the unwanted interference that accompanies a signal, a filter is needed.\r\n\r\n<h3>Analogue filters</h3>\r\n<h3>Digital filters</h3>\r\n\r\nClassigfication of filters:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Low pass filters</li>\r\n<li>High pass filters</li>\r\n<li>Band-pass filters</li>\r\n<li>Band-reject filters</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nClassigfication of filters:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Continuous time</li>\r\n<li>Dscrete time</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nClassigfication of filters:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Passive filters</li>\r\n<li>Active filters</li>\r\n</ul>",
