    "chapter": "Sensors and Transducers",
    "topic": "LVDT",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class=\"note-split-grid\" style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; align-items: start; width: 100%;\">\n\t<div class=\"note-text-col\" style=\"min-width: 0;\">\n\n<p>A Linear Variable Differential Transducer (LVDT) is a widely used electromechanical sensor that measures linear displacement or position changes.</p>\n\n<p>Linear Variable Differential Transducers (LVDTs) are precise and reliable sensors commonly employed for measuring linear displacement. They operate on the principle of electromagnetic induction and are extensively used in industries such as automotive, aerospace, manufacturing, and robotics.</p>\n\n<h5><span><b>Key Components:</b></span></h5>\nAn LVDT consists of three primary components:\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Primary Coil:</strong> The primary coil is typically wound around a hollow cylindrical core made of ferromagnetic material. Alternating current (AC) is applied to this coil, creating an electromagnetic field within the core.</li>\n\n<li><strong>Secondary Coils:</strong> There are two secondary coils, symmetrically positioned on either side of the primary coil. These coils are connected in series but wound in opposite directions. When the core moves, it induces an electromotive force (EMF) in these coils, creating a differential output.</li>\n\n<li><strong>Movable Core (Armature):</strong> The core, also known as the armature, is a ferromagnetic rod placed inside the primary coil. It is free to move axially within the core.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h5><span><b>Working Principle:</b></span></h5>\n<ol>\n<li>When no external force is applied, the core rests at the null position, equidistant from both secondary coils.</li>\n<li>When an object or mechanism moves the core, it changes the coupling between the primary and secondary coils. As a result, the induced EMF in the two secondary coils becomes imbalanced.</li>\n<li>The difference in the EMF outputs from the secondary coils is proportional to the displacement of the core. This differential output is used to determine the linear position or displacement of the core with high accuracy.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h5><span><b>Advantages of LVDT:</b></span></h5>\n<ol>\n<li>High accuracy and precision in measuring linear displacement.</li>\n<li>Excellent linearity and repeatability.</li>\n<li>Long-term stability and durability.</li>\n<li>Immune to vibration and shock.</li>\n<li>Insensitive to temperature variations.</li>\n<li>Provides absolute position information.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h5><span><b>Applications:</b></span></h5>\nLVDTs find applications in various industries, including:\n<ol>\n<li>Aerospace: Used for position feedback in aircraft control surfaces and landing gear.</li>\n<li>Automotive: Employed in engine control systems and suspension systems.</li>\n<li>Manufacturing: Used for quality control and measurement in machining processes.</li>\n<li>Civil Engineering: Applied in structural health monitoring and geotechnical instrumentation.</li>\n<li>Medical Devices: Utilized in medical imaging and diagnostic equipment.</li>\n</ol>\n\t</div>\n\n\t<div class=\"note-media-col\" style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; align-items: center; min-width: 0;\">\n        <div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\">\n            <img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/d/1EMP4VqIVLLmrZcOSPFNMDv6MPzl1YKGh\" alt=\"Industrial LVDT Linear Displacement Transducer\" style=\"max-width: 100%; max-height: 320px; width: auto; height: auto; object-fit: contain; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); cursor: pointer;\" onclick=\"if(window.showPhotoLightbox) window.showPhotoLightbox(this.src);\" title=\"Click to view full image\"><br/>\n            <small class=\"text-muted\" style=\"display: block; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 500;\"><strong>Industrial LVDT Sensor</strong> with cylindrical housing, movable core shaft & lead wires</small>\n        </div>\n        <div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: center; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.02); border-radius: 12px; padding: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\">\n            <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/Lvdt_how.gif\" alt=\"LVDT Working Principle Animation\" style=\"max-width: 100%; max-height: 260px; width: auto; height: auto; object-fit: contain; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\"><br/>\n            <small style=\"display: block; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 0.78rem;\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lvdt_how.gif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: inherit; text-decoration: underline;\">Fenixdiaz</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons</small>\n        </div>\n\t</div>\n</div>",
