    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Probability and Statistics",
    "chapter": "Laws of Probability",
    "topic": "Probability - Basic Concepts",
    "subtopic": "Conditional Probability",
    "content_html": "<p><strong>Conditional probability</strong> is a measure of the probability of an event given that another event has already occurred.</p>\r\n\\[P(A/B) = \\dfrac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}\\]\r\n\r\n\\[P(A/B) = P(A)\\]\r\nThat means the fact that event B has taken place, makes no difference for occurance of event A.<br/>\r\nFor independent events,\r\n\\[P(A \\cap B) = P(A). P(B)\\]",
    "important": "Permutations\r\n\\[P(n,r) = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\]\r\nCombinations\r\n\\[C(n,r) = \\dfrac{n!}{r!(n-r)!}\\]\r\n\r\n\\[P(A) = \\dfrac{n(A)}{n(S)}\\]\r\n\\[0 \\leq P(A) \\leq 1\\]\r\n\r\n\\[P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qjJA_8rFbZMStA_nT1PKeYnjZq4W7wNG/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900/40 text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-200 transition-colors\">📄 Homework</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1yTluxRwTDaMfJub5KR2454R-9Jo-DxOR/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-900/40 text-green-700 dark:text-green-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-green-200 transition-colors\">✅ Solution</a><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1hipwAXK7oALPLqnqZRhi2k1z023t1fSr/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
