    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Probability and Statistics",
    "chapter": "Probability Functions, Distributions, and Expected Values",
    "topic": "PDF and CDF",
    "subtopic": "Cumulative Distribution Function",
    "content_html": "<h5><b>Cumulative Distribution Function:</b></h5>\r\n\r\nIf X is continuous, the <strong>probability density function</strong>, f, is defined such that:</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$P( -\\infty \\leq X \\leq b) = \\displaystyle \\int_{-\\infty}^b f(x) dx$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 65</span></button>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>The <strong>cumulative distribution function</strong>, F, of a discrete random variable X that has a probability distribution described by P(x<span class=\"math inline\">\\(_i\\)</span>) is defined as: \r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$F(x_m) = \\Sigma P(x_k) = P(X \\leq x_m), m = 1,2,...,n$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 65</span></button>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "Cumulative Distribution Function:\r\n\\[F(x_m) = P(X \\leq x_m) = \\displaystyle \\int_{-\\infty}^{x_m} f(x) dx\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1R8obz-ri6xpLjdkxlR46DopwZXq_llcE/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
