    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Safety, Health, and Environment",
    "chapter": "Industrial Hygiene",
    "topic": "Exposure Limits",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p><b>Exposure:</b> The extent of contact with the proposed causative agent (or its proxy) in a risk relationship.</p>\r\n\r\nExposure assessment deals with:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Percentage of population or workforce exposed</li>\r\n<li>Sources of exposure</li>\r\n<li>Pathways of exposure</li>\r\n<li>Approprite measure of dose</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nGeneral formula for Average daily dose:\r\n\\[ADD = \\dfrac{C \\times IR \\times T \\times AF}{BW \\times AT}\\]\r\n(Source: George Washington University, DC, Center for Risk Science and Public Health)\r\nwhere, <br/>\r\nADD = Average Daily Dose<br/>\r\nC= Concentration<br/>\r\nIR = Intake Rate<br/>\r\nT = Time or duration of exposure<br/>\r\nAF = Absorption (bioavailability Factor<br/>\r\nBW = Body Weight<br/>\r\nAT = Averaging Time<br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Hierarchy_of_Occupational_Exposure_Limits.JPG\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hierarchy_of_Occupational_Exposure_Limits.JPG\">Exposurescientist</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
