    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Safety, Health, and Environment",
    "chapter": "Basic Safety Equipment",
    "topic": "Fire Prevention and Control",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "Fire Prevention:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Fire Codes and Regulations: Understanding and adhering to local and national fire codes and regulations is essential for preventing fires. Codes often cover building design, occupancy limits, fire alarms, and more.</li>\r\n<li>Fire Safety in Buildings: Proper building design and maintenance are essential to minimize fire risks. This includes fire-resistant construction materials, sprinkler systems, fire alarms, and emergency exits.</li>\r\n<li>Fire Safety Planning: Developing and implementing a comprehensive fire safety plan is crucial. This plan should include evacuation procedures, fire drills, and communication systems.</li>\r\n<li>Fire Safety Equipment: Fire extinguishers, fire blankets, and other firefighting equipment should be readily available and maintained in good working condition.</li>\r\n<li>Fire Suppression Systems: Automatic fire suppression systems like sprinklers and fire suppression agents are effective in controlling fires in their early stages.</li>\r\n</ul>",
