    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Statics",
    "chapter": "Systems of Forces",
    "topic": "Equilibrium of Rigid Bodies",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Types of Supports:</b></span></h5>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   Roller Support: Offers reaction only in one direction.\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/Loslager.png\" style=\"max-width: 10vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Loslager.png\">The original uploader was Madras at German Wikipedia.</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n<li><div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   Hinge Support: Offers reaction in two directions.\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/61/Festlager.png\" style=\"max-width: 10vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Festlager.png\">The original uploader was Madras at German Wikipedia.</a>, Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n<hr>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<li><div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n Fixed Support: Offers reaction in two directions AND offers resisting moment.\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/Fixed_support_02.svg\" style=\"max-width: 10vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fixed_support_02.svg\">Oimabe</a>, CC0, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <h5><span><b>Types of Loads:</b></span></h5>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Point Load:</li>\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/Simple_beam_with_offset_load.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simple_beam_with_offset_load.svg\">Hermanoere</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n<li>Uniformly Distributed Load: (UDL)</li>\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Simple_beam_with_uniform_distributed_load.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simple_beam_with_uniform_distributed_load.svg\">Hermanoere</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n<li>Triangular Load (Uniformly Varying Load):</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Conditions for Static Equilibrium:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container-fluid\">\r\n\t<div class=\"row align-items-start\">\r\n\t\t<div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n\r\n<p><span class=\"math display\">\\[\\sum F_x = 0,\\ \\sum F_y = 0,\\ \\sum F_z = 0\\]</span> <span class=\"math display\">\\[\\sum M_x = 0,\\ \\sum M_y = 0,\\ \\sum M_z = 0\\]</span> If a problem is in 2-D only then only three conditions will remain. \r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\sum F_x = 0,\\ \\sum F_y = 0,\\ \\sum M = 0$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 94</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n\t\t</div>\r\n    \t\t<div class=\"col\">\r\n    <center> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/STATICS-RBSE01-01-01-bf088330985843ba943c45d958be718c0.png\" alt=\"Equilibrium\" width=\"340\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STATICS-RBSE01-01-01-bf088330985843ba943c45d958be718c0.png\">Brina Schenk with UBC and Douglas College</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\">CC BY 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    \t\t</div>\r\n  \t</div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "For 3-D:\r\n\\[\\sum F_x = 0,\\ \\sum F_y = 0,\\ \\sum F_z = 0\\]\r\n\\[\\sum M_x = 0,\\ \\sum M_y = 0,\\ \\sum M_z = 0\\]\r\n\r\nFor 2-D:\r\n\\[\\sum F_x = 0,\\ \\sum F_y = 0,\\ \\sum M = 0\\]\r\n\r\n\\[\\dfrac{F_1}{\\sin\\ \\alpha} = \\dfrac{F_2}{\\sin\\ \\beta} = \\dfrac{F_3}{\\sin\\ \\gamma}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10WJ7VURrhRrR9wSUabVNaw6sxTgHzJLh/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
