    "content_html": "<p>The enthalpy of formation (<span class=\"math inline\">\\(\\Delta\\)</span> H<span class=\"math inline\">\\(_f\\)</span>) is the increase in enthalpy when a compound is formed from its constituent elements in their natural form and in a standard state. The standard state is 25<span class=\"math inline\">\\(^\\circ\\)</span>C and 1 atm. pressure.</p>",
