    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer",
    "chapter": "Conduction",
    "topic": "Lumped System Analysis",
    "subtopic": "Approximate Solution for Solid with Sudden Convection",
    "content_html": "<p>When Bi number is greater than 0.1, lumped system analysis yields inaccurate results. In such case, One-term approximation can be used. First Biot number is calculated using the following formulae.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5><b>For Plane Wall</b></h5>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$Bi = \\dfrac{hL}{k}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 208</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<h5><b>For Infinite Cylinder and Sphere</b></h5>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n  <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$Bi = \\dfrac{hr_0}{k}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 208</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n<p>In this method, standard tables are referred from page 208, to get the coefficients, $\\zeta_1$ and C$_1$ depending upon object type and Biot number.</p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dfrac{(T_0 - T_{\\infty})}{(T_i- T_{\\infty})} = C_1 exp (-\\zeta_1^2 Fo)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 207</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>",
    "important": "\\[Bi = \\dfrac{h L_c}{k}\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fTrZXq7C_7607mKD5wr_Ixg7IBxLGmxA/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
    "images": [],
    "local_images": []
