    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer",
    "chapter": "Nonreacting Mixtures of Gases",
    "topic": "Nonreacting Mixtures of Gases",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Mass and Mole Fractions:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Mole fraction, (x$_i$): the ratio of the mole number of a component to the mole number of the mixture.</li>\r\n<li>Mass fraction, (y$_i$): the ratio of the mass of a component to the mass of the mixture.</li>\r\n\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Conversion between Mass and Mole Fractions:</b></span></h5>\r\nTo convert mole fractions x$_i$ to mass fractions y$_i$:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$y_i = \\dfrac{x_iM_i}{\\Sigma x_i M_i}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 145</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\nTo convert mass fractions to mole fractions:\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$x_i = \\dfrac{\\dfrac{y_i}{M_i}}{\\Sigma \\left( \\dfrac{y_i}{M_i}\\right)}$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 145</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<p>To use specific properties, such enthalpy, internal energy, entropy and both specific heats, use mass fraction.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To find masses involved in chemical reactions and to find pressure and volume, use mole fraction.</p>\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Dalton's Law of Partial Pressures:</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p>The pressure of a mixture of gases is the sum of the partial pressures of its components when each alone occupies the volume of the mixture, V, at the temperature, T, of the mixture. <span class=\"math display\">\\[P_{\\mathrm{Total}} = P_1 + P_2 + P_3 + .....\\]</span></p>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$P = \\Sigma P_i$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 145</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>",
    "important": "\\[y_i = \\dfrac{x_iM_i}{\\Sigma x_i M_i}\\]\r\n\r\n\\[x_i = \\dfrac{\\dfrac{y_i}{M_i}}{\\Sigma \\left( \\dfrac{y_i}{M_i}\\right)}\\]\r\n\r\n\\[P_{\\mathrm{Total}} = P_1 + P_2 + P_3 + .....\\]",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bA5ByGpc70vKsgTFZ9g81_UfsNKr3jSN/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
