    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer",
    "chapter": "Property and Phase Diagram",
    "topic": "P-h Diagrams",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n    <div class=\"col-8\">\r\n   <ul>\r\n<li>Pressure is on y-axis and Enthalpy is on x-axis.</li>\r\n<li>The top most point is the critical point.</li>\r\n<li>The left side curve represents x= 0 whereas the right side curve represents x=1</li>\r\n<li>The area between the left and right curve is saturated region (liquid-vapor mixture) and you will have to refer <b>Saturated Water - Temperature Table</b> on page 157 of the handbook.</li>\r\n<li>The area to the right of (beyond) right curve is superheated region and you will have to refer <b>Superheated Water Tables</b> on page 157 of the handbook.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center>\r\n<img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Pressure-enthalpy_chart_for_steam%2C_in_US_units.svg\" alt=\"Pressure-enthalpy chart\" width=\"500\"><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pressure-enthalpy_chart_for_steam,_in_US_units.svg\">Emok</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
