    "topic": "Net Energy Exchange by Radiation between Two Bodies",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <p>Radiation is different than other two modes of heat transfer, (conduction and convection), because radiation does not require medium for heat transfer. </p>\r\n\r\n<p>This means irrespective of the surrounding medium, a body is continuously emitting radiation heat to the surroundings which is proportional to the fourth power of its abolute (Kelvin) temperature)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Let us consider two bodies having unequal temperatures. Body 1 with temperature T$_1$ and Body 2 with temperature T$_2$. Let us assume T$_1$ > T$_2$. This means Body 1 is continuously emitting radiation heat $\\dot Q_{1} = \\epsilon \\sigma A \\left(T_1^4\\right)$ and Body 2 is continuously emitting radiation heat $\\dot Q_{2} = \\epsilon \\sigma A \\left(T_1^4\\right)$ since T$_1$ is assumed to be higher than T$_2$, Q$_1$ will be higher than Q$_2$. In such case, body 1 will have a net gain of radiation heat and body 2 will have a net loss of radiation heat, and both values will be given by:</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\dot Q_{12} = \\epsilon \\sigma A \\left(T_1^4 - T_2 ^4\\right)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 218</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Heat-transfer-between-thermodynamic-systems.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heat-transfer-between-thermodynamic-systems.svg\">MikeRun</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons</small></small></center><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>",
    "important": "",
    "resources": "<div class=\"mt-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/11ZBhqYCfE0EOQ8q6nPqAYrNHRXNJGmwC/preview\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-100 dark:bg-purple-900/40 text-purple-700 dark:text-purple-300 rounded text-xs font-bold hover:bg-purple-200 transition-colors\">👨‍🏫 Tutoring</a></div>",
