    "discipline": "Other",
    "subject": "Thermodynamics and Heat Transfer",
    "chapter": "Second Law of Thermodynamics",
    "topic": "Exergy (Availability)",
    "subtopic": "Overview",
    "content_html": "<h5><span><b>Exergy (Availability):</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<p>Exergy (also known as availability) is the maximum possible work that can be obtained from a cycle of a heat engine. The maximum possible work is obtained in a reversible process.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class= \"container-fluid\">\r\n  <div class= \"row align-items-start\">\r\n   <div class=\"col col-lg-8\">\r\n   <h5><span><b>Closed-System Exergy (Availability):</b></span></h5>\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\phi = (u - u_L) - T_L(s-s_L) + p_L (v-v_L)$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 152</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$w_{max} = w_{rev} = \\phi_i - \\phi_2$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 152</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <div class=\"col\">\r\n<center><p><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Carnot_cycle_TS_diagram.svg\" style=\"max-width: 50vh;\"></p><br/>\r\n<small><small><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carnot_cycle_TS_diagram.svg\">Setreset</a>, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via Wikimedia Commons<br/></small></small></center>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n<h5><span><b>Open-System Exergy (Availability):</b></span></h5>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$\\psi = (h - h_L) - T_L(s-s_L) + \\dfrac{V^2}{2} + gZ$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 152</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-center\">\r\n<button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-light shadow-lg\">$w_{max} = w_{rev} = \\psi_1 - \\psi_2$ <span class=\"text-muted\">&emsp; &emsp; &emsp; Page 152</span></button>\r\n</div><br/>",
    "important": "",
